<div class="main-process-safety allServeDetails section-gap">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-md-6">
                <div class="process-img">
                    <img src="/images/serviceimages/hazardandoperability.jpg" alt="Process Safety Management (PSM)" class="img-fluid" loading="lazy" width="670" height="475">
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
                <div class="process-content specialset">
                    <h3><span>What is PSM?</span></h3>
                    <p>Process Safety Management (PSM) is a comprehensive approach to managing the risks associated with hazardous chemicals and processes, ensuring the safety of people, equipment, and the environment. By implementing a structured and proactive system, PSM aims to prevent accidents, minimize exposure to risks, and protect assets throughout the entire lifecycle of industrial operations.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="row" style="margin-top:50px;">
            <div class="col-md-12">
                <div class="text-center">
                    <div data-aos="zoom-in" data-aos-easing="linear" data-aos-duration="800">
                        <div class="heading mb-50">
                            <h2>Key Elements of <span> PSM</span></h2>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-12" data-aos="fade-up">
                <div class="process-content specialset innerMainPara">
                    <p><span>Process Hazard Analysis (PHA):</span> Identifying and evaluating potential hazards and risks within processes, systems, and operations.</p>
                    <p><span>Operating Procedures: </span> Developing clear, detailed procedures for safe operations and emergency response.</p>
                    <p><span>Mechanical Integrity: </span> Ensuring the reliability and safety of equipment through regular inspection, maintenance, and testing.</p>
                    <p><span>Training and Competency: </span> Providing ongoing training to ensure all personnel understand and follow safety procedures.</p>
                    <p><span>Emergency Planning and Response: </span>Establishing effective plans for responding to process-related emergencies to minimize harm.</p>
                    <p><span>Management of Change (MOC): </span>Ensuring safe handling of any changes in processes, technology, or personnel that could affect safety.</p>
                    <p><span>Incident Investigation: </span>Investigating accidents, near misses, and safety concerns to identify root causes and implement corrective actions.</p>
                    <p><span>Audit and Continuous Improvement:</span> Regularly auditing the safety management system and continuously improving safety practices.</p>

                    <p><span>Process Safety Management (PSM)</span> is crucial because it protects both people and assets by minimizing the risk of accidents that could harm employees, contractors, and the surrounding community. It ensures regulatory compliance by meeting the requirements set by OSHA (Occupational Safety and Health Administration) and other relevant regulatory bodies. PSM also helps reduce operational downtime by preventing safety incidents that could disrupt operations and lead to costly delays. Moreover, it promotes a safety culture by embedding safety into every aspect of the organization’s operations, fostering a proactive approach to risk management.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="col-md-12" style="margin-top:50px;">
                    <div class="text-center">
                        <div data-aos="zoom-in" data-aos-easing="linear" data-aos-duration="800">
